From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:48:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] net/netmon,wgengine: offer CGNAT LAN endpoints for registered
 tunnels

An address on another eligible interface can be a direct IPv4 path on
a shared CGNAT LAN. Preserve tunnel exclusion by name and conservative
IPv6 eligibility. The daemon and relay explicitly select their range
policy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
---
 cmd/tailscaled/tailscaled.go    |  2 ++
 net/netmon/interfaces_test.go   | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 net/netmon/state.go             | 12 +++++------
 net/udprelay/server.go          |  2 +-
 tsnet/tsnet.go                  |  2 ++
 wgengine/magicsock/magicsock.go |  7 +++++-
 wgengine/userspace.go           |  5 +++++
 7 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

